    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Renaming maps architectural registers onto a larger physical register file.",
      "narration": "Rename removes false dependencies. Each new destination gets a fresh physical register, so write-after-write and write-after-read hazards vanish, and only true data dependencies remain.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Register renaming",
